# AI Developer's Launch Pad V2 - Development Plan

## Project Overview
This document outlines the development plan for transforming the AI Developer's Launch Pad into a MongoDB-branded, production-ready template for modern web applications.

## Phase 0: Cleanup and Preparation
- [ ] Analyze existing codebase thoroughly
- [ ] Identify legacy files and components to be removed
- [ ] Create a backup of the current state
- [ ] Document dependencies and their purposes
-

## Phase 1: Core Architecture Transformation
- [ ] Implement feature-based folder organization
- [ ] Separate business logic from UI components
- [ ] Create clear boundaries between server and client components
- [ ] Optimize MongoDB connection with proper pooling and error handling
- [ ] Enhance Auth0 integration with better token management

## Phase 2: MongoDB-Inspired Design System
- [ ] Implement MongoDB's color palette (primary: #00ED64)
- [ ] Create MongoDB-styled UI components using Shadcn UI
- [ ] Design MongoDB Atlas dashboard-inspired layouts
- [ ] Implement consistent dark mode based on MongoDB Cloud interface
- [ ] Add subtle animations and transitions for better UX

## Phase 3: Enhanced Data Management
- [ ] Implement robust Mongoose models with validation
- [ ] Create optimized API routes with proper error handling
- [ ] Add data fetching layer with SWR or React Query
- [ ] Implement MongoDB aggregation pipeline examples
- [ ] Add proper indexing strategies for MongoDB collections

## Phase 4: Authentication and Security
- [ ] Enhance Auth0 integration with role-based access control
- [ ] Create middleware for protected routes
- [ ] Implement proper token refresh handling
- [ ] Add session management utilities
- [ ] Create comprehensive security headers

## Phase 5: UI Implementation
- [ ] Build MongoDB-inspired dashboard layout
- [ ] Create reusable components with MongoDB styling
- [ ] Implement responsive design for all viewport sizes
- [ ] Add data visualization components
- [ ] Implement form handling with React Hook Form

## Phase 6: Testing and Documentation
- [ ] Implement Jest/React Testing Library tests
- [ ] Add end-to-end testing with Cypress
- [ ] Create comprehensive component documentation
- [ ] Document API endpoints and usage
- [ ] Add example implementations and use cases

## Phase 7: Optimization and Deployment
- [ ] Optimize bundle sizes and performance
- [ ] Implement proper error boundaries and fallbacks
- [ ] Add analytics integration
- [ ] Create CI/CD pipeline
- [ ] Prepare deployment documentation

## Development Rules

### Code Structure
- Use feature-based folder organization
- Separate server and client components clearly
- Follow naming conventions consistently
- Keep components focused and single-purpose
- Use TypeScript with strict typing

### MongoDB Integration
- Always use connection pooling
- Implement proper error handling for database operations
- Use Mongoose for data modeling
- Add proper indexing for collections
- Validate data before database operations

### Authentication
- Never use Edge Runtime with Auth0
- Always handle token expiration
- Implement proper logout cleanup
- Use secure session cookies
- Add proper error handling for auth failures

### UI Components
- Follow MongoDB design guidelines
- Use Tailwind CSS for styling
- Create responsive designs for all components
- Implement proper loading states
- Add error boundaries for component failures

### State Management
- Use React Query or SWR for server state
- Implement Zustand or Jotai for client state
- Keep state management simple and predictable
- Avoid prop drilling with context where appropriate
- Document state management patterns

### Testing
- Write tests for all components
- Test error states and edge cases
- Implement end-to-end tests for critical flows
- Mock external dependencies in tests
- Aim for high test coverage

## Important Notes
- Do not start actual development until explicit permission is given
- Clean up legacy files only after confirmation
- Document all major changes
- Follow MongoDB branding guidelines
- Prioritize performance and user experience